From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:45:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/UsbBusDxe: Free BOS buffer on read failure

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0049, as it is]

UsbGetDevBosDesc() allocates a buffer for the initial BOS descriptor
request. If that request fails, the success-only cleanup is skipped and
the function returns without freeing the buffer. Repeated enumeration
attempts can leak one allocation per failure.

Free the initial buffer before returning the transfer error.

The leaking retrieval helper was introduced by PR #12714:
https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/pull/12714

Signed-off-by: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>

ouroBIOS backport of tianocore/edk2 commit 52fa6fe8996f (merged on
2026-10-21, after edk2-stable202608, the base of MrChromebox's
uefipayload_2608), applied unchanged. Drop it when the base includes
it.

Why here: the third fix, after 0047 and 0048, to the BOS code of PR
#12714 in the base: a device whose BOS request failed left one
allocation behind at every attempt to enumerate it.

TEST=git am on the series: clean, at another offset (MrChromebox's
UsbDesc.c moves it), the same lines as upstream.
---
 MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c | 49 ++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c
index be43bea7b..c12170954 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c
@@ -742,32 +742,41 @@ UsbGetDevBosDesc (
              Buf,
              sizeof (EFI_USB_BOS_DESCRIPTOR)
              );
-  if (!EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-    TotalLength = ((EFI_USB_BOS_DESCRIPTOR *)Buf)->TotalLength;
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
     gBS->FreePool (Buf);
-    Buf = NULL;
-    Buf = AllocateZeroPool (TotalLength);
-    if (Buf == NULL) {
-      return EFI_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
-    }
+    return Status;
+  }
 
-    Status = UsbCtrlGetDesc (
-               UsbDev,
-               USB_DESC_TYPE_BOS,
-               0,
-               0,
-               Buf,
-               TotalLength
-               );
+  TotalLength = ((EFI_USB_BOS_DESCRIPTOR *)Buf)->TotalLength;
 
-    if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-      gBS->FreePool (Buf);
-      Buf = NULL;
-    }
+  // The reported BOS length must include its fixed header before allocating.
+  if (TotalLength < sizeof (EFI_USB_BOS_DESCRIPTOR)) {
+    gBS->FreePool (Buf);
+    return EFI_DEVICE_ERROR;
+  }
 
-    UsbDev->DevDesc->BosDesc = (EFI_USB_BOS_DESCRIPTOR *)Buf;
+  gBS->FreePool (Buf);
+  Buf = NULL;
+  Buf = AllocateZeroPool (TotalLength);
+  if (Buf == NULL) {
+    return EFI_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
+  }
+
+  Status = UsbCtrlGetDesc (
+             UsbDev,
+             USB_DESC_TYPE_BOS,
+             0,
+             0,
+             Buf,
+             TotalLength
+             );
+
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    gBS->FreePool (Buf);
+    Buf = NULL;
   }
 
+  UsbDev->DevDesc->BosDesc = (EFI_USB_BOS_DESCRIPTOR *)Buf;
   return Status;
 }
 
